00:27:35.040 --> 00:27:37.630
Doing it is a bunch of chaotic steps.

00:27:37.630 --> 00:27:38.570
It now looks neat.

00:27:38.570 --> 00:27:43.310
[LAUGH] But I mean, doing it are a series
of trials and err-, trial and error.

00:27:43.310 --> 00:27:46.090
This is codifying everything I know.

00:27:46.090 --> 00:27:48.260
I think I've, I've learned more in the
last 3

00:27:48.260 --> 00:27:50.320
years than I learned in the first 40 at
work.

00:27:50.320 --> 00:27:50.790
&gt;&gt; Really?

00:27:50.790 --> 00:27:55.360
&gt;&gt; Just by understanding what I did, or
what we did.

00:27:55.360 --> 00:27:57.110
How people responded.

00:27:57.110 --> 00:27:58.450
What worked and didn't work?

00:27:58.450 --> 00:28:01.610
I mean, when you're, when you're doing it,
you're in the battlefield.

00:28:02.810 --> 00:28:05.440
Shrapnel's coming from all sides.

00:28:05.440 --> 00:28:07.900
You're not thinking through a lot of these
moves.

00:28:07.900 --> 00:28:12.320
I think hopefully, this book will give
people some insights that can be useful.

00:28:12.320 --> 00:28:17.610
I mean I, I'm a lot smarter writing it
today than I was when I started.

00:28:18.730 --> 00:28:21.150
So I'm I'd say that I've learned a hell of
a lot now.

00:28:22.500 --> 00:28:23.640
&gt;&gt; Thank you very much for being here
again.

