00:49:28.400 --> 00:49:32.015
I don't mean to be aggressive here but
that's what your job is.

00:49:32.015 --> 00:49:35.777
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH] I was hoping you could share

00:49:35.777 --> 00:49:41.430
some insight into how you manage your own
time.

00:49:41.430 --> 00:49:43.380
Particularly when you were heading a large
company.

00:49:43.380 --> 00:49:45.040
I'm sure everybody wants a piece of the

00:49:45.040 --> 00:49:48.080
CEO, everybody wants to talk to the
chairman.

00:49:48.080 --> 00:49:51.030
&gt;&gt; You know, I, I knew what my job was.

00:49:51.030 --> 00:49:55.540
I really understood that my job was not
managing to find

00:49:55.540 --> 00:50:00.650
a new comedy, build a jet engine, I build
a medical scanner.

00:50:00.650 --> 00:50:02.910
And within, it's an impossible job.

00:50:04.010 --> 00:50:07.800
But I knew my job was building people,
building talent.

00:50:07.800 --> 00:50:11.910
And I came to work every day thinking
about the people process.

00:50:11.910 --> 00:50:15.410
And thinking about evaluations, when I
went to factories, I sat down

00:50:15.410 --> 00:50:18.440
with the union and talked with them about
how things were going.

00:50:18.440 --> 00:50:20.180
More to find out what the atmosphere in
the

00:50:20.180 --> 00:50:23.520
place was than to find out the specific,
specific grief.

00:50:23.520 --> 00:50:28.631
So, my job, if I, if we didn't build all
these leaders, that now we

00:50:28.631 --> 00:50:33.850
have 35 or so, for, Fortune 500 CEOs and
for the Dow Jones 30.

00:50:33.850 --> 00:50:37.050
If we didn't do that, we would have
failed.

00:50:37.050 --> 00:50:40.017
Cuz my job was not coming up with a,
Seinfeld com,

00:50:40.017 --> 00:50:43.490
comedy or a, an apprentice show, or any of
these things.

00:50:43.490 --> 00:50:50.230
My job was to get somebody to run that
place, who will come up with those things.

00:50:50.230 --> 00:50:52.040
So my time, which I'll say, 65% to 75% on
that.

00:50:52.040 --> 00:50:54.350
I have three things I had to do.

00:50:54.350 --> 00:50:56.400
I had to, pick people.

00:50:58.130 --> 00:51:01.240
I had to, allocate resources, based on
what

00:51:01.240 --> 00:51:03.410
the people were selling me, eyeball to
eyeball.

00:51:05.160 --> 00:51:06.930
And I had to transfer good ideas.

00:51:07.940 --> 00:51:09.590
Generic ideas across the business.

00:51:09.590 --> 00:51:10.450
That's all I did.

00:51:10.450 --> 00:51:11.930
I didn't have any pricing power.

00:51:11.930 --> 00:51:14.140
Any, design issues.

00:51:14.140 --> 00:51:15.740
Any of those things, I knew my job.

00:51:15.740 --> 00:51:19.770
And so I allocated most of my time to
people.

00:51:19.770 --> 00:51:20.270
&gt;&gt; Thanks.

00:51:22.420 --> 00:51:25.390
Dr. Welsh, I have a question on the
appraisal system.

00:51:25.390 --> 00:51:25.880
&gt;&gt; Yep.

00:51:25.880 --> 00:51:28.420
&gt;&gt; specifically, the grading curve we
talked about.

00:51:28.420 --> 00:51:31.180
And you mentioned earlier, that, spend a
lot of

00:51:31.180 --> 00:51:35.260
time just doing whatever to keep the top
20%.

00:51:35.260 --> 00:51:39.271
For the next middle 70% you kinda tell
them to be the top 20%

00:51:39.271 --> 00:51:43.440
and the bottom 10% kinda help them out but
help them out as well.

00:51:45.410 --> 00:51:48.490
What I struggle with that it seems to be a

00:51:48.490 --> 00:51:52.870
zero sum game the moment you put it in
relative terms.

00:51:52.870 --> 00:51:56.210
The 70, middle 70% cannot make it to the
top 20%

00:51:56.210 --> 00:52:01.591
without someone in a top 20% falling out
into the middle 70%.

00:52:01.591 --> 00:52:05.500
In terms of the actual application of this
system, is

00:52:05.500 --> 00:52:08.490
there, is it, does it work because GE is
so large?

00:52:08.490 --> 00:52:12.930
Because if you tried it to, to implement
it in a small enough division or unit.

00:52:12.930 --> 00:52:15.450
You may actually lose a lot of good
people.

00:52:15.450 --> 00:52:18.082
&gt;&gt; Yeah, but, aren't, aren't you raiding
the bar all the time?

00:52:18.082 --> 00:52:18.582
&gt;&gt; Yes.

00:52:20.340 --> 00:52:20.650
&gt;&gt; Right.

00:52:20.650 --> 00:52:25.760
&gt;&gt; Tell me a better system to raise the
bar, all, all of the group.

00:52:25.760 --> 00:52:27.020
Give me an alternative.

00:52:28.410 --> 00:52:31.620
This is one I got that I think is one of
the best that I've come up with.

00:52:31.620 --> 00:52:33.630
I don't say that it's the only one.

00:52:33.630 --> 00:52:34.640
It what I believe is better.

00:52:34.640 --> 00:52:38.110
Now you tell me a better one to get a
better chain.

00:52:38.110 --> 00:52:41.110
&gt;&gt; I believe that the message is sending a
good vibe.

00:52:41.110 --> 00:52:45.573
But what I'm, what I'm uncomfortable with
is the, the bottom 10% even

00:52:45.573 --> 00:52:50.005
if they have improved in absolute terms,
we would still be asked to leave.

00:52:50.005 --> 00:52:52.709
Is, is it not [INAUDIBLE] in, in practice?

00:52:52.709 --> 00:52:54.216
&gt;&gt; Oh, it's not, I mean, you're not,

00:52:54.216 --> 00:52:56.300
you're not, down there with a fine tooth
comb.

00:52:56.300 --> 00:52:58.420
This is all directional.

00:52:58.420 --> 00:53:02.280
But clearly you wanna get the, you don't
wanna spend quality.

00:53:02.280 --> 00:53:06.240
It's like ha, ha, ha, having the bad egg
on the play, playground.

00:53:06.240 --> 00:53:11.440
You don't wanna spend your time trying to
take somebody that's not very good.

00:53:11.440 --> 00:53:13.876
And, you wanna take great people and make

00:53:13.876 --> 00:53:16.950
the unbelievably great, that's what your
job is.

00:53:16.950 --> 00:53:19.163
If you waste time trying to get someone

00:53:19.163 --> 00:53:22.346
over the bottom ten thresholds, you'll be
spending a

00:53:22.346 --> 00:53:24.836
lot of energy on something that's not very

00:53:24.836 --> 00:53:28.950
productive, and they can and they'll do
find elsewhere.

00:53:28.950 --> 00:53:30.490
If you do it early enough in their career.

00:53:31.630 --> 00:53:34.710
So, so I just think it's the best way to
do it.

00:53:34.710 --> 00:53:37.800
I, I, but, I, I would never sit here in
say, this is the only way.

00:53:37.800 --> 00:53:42.300
And you get it by saying, I don't like
this because after, after I do it twice.

00:53:42.300 --> 00:53:45.379
I've already gotten rid, rid of the weak
people, now, now I've got a perfect team.

00:53:46.650 --> 00:53:49.350
That's not true because what'll happen is
you'll get promoted

00:53:49.350 --> 00:53:52.060
because you'll have a great team and if
you don't

00:53:52.060 --> 00:53:55.060
keep doing it, somebody else is gonna into
your job

00:53:55.060 --> 00:53:58.420
and they're gonna say, what, and what is
your, your name?

00:53:58.420 --> 00:54:00.390
What is your name?

00:54:00.390 --> 00:54:01.130
Ron, Don.

00:54:02.380 --> 00:54:03.670
So they're gonna take Don.

00:54:03.670 --> 00:54:04.680
Don, Don got promoted.

00:54:04.680 --> 00:54:06.210
He went to another place.

00:54:06.210 --> 00:54:08.774
And then they come to Don's job and
[CROSSTALK]

00:54:08.774 --> 00:54:11.824
well, and they're gonna look at the
people, okay?

00:54:11.824 --> 00:54:13.889
They're gonna look at the people.

00:54:13.889 --> 00:54:18.800
And they're gonna say they are gonna do a
top 20 middle 70 bottom 10.

00:54:18.800 --> 00:54:21.380
They're gonna say, my God how did he keep
that person?

00:54:22.380 --> 00:54:24.450
So you're not doing anyone any favors
because

00:54:24.450 --> 00:54:26.860
fresh eyes will look at it differently
every time.

00:54:28.340 --> 00:54:31.180
And so I just think it's the best way to
build a team.

00:54:31.180 --> 00:54:34.490
But I do not say it's the only way to
build a team.

00:54:34.490 --> 00:54:37.850
I found it to be a clear-cut, it forced

00:54:37.850 --> 00:54:43.620
evaluations, it forced people to stop
winking at people, it

00:54:43.620 --> 00:54:47.540
was transparent, and people knew they got
a fair shake,

00:54:47.540 --> 00:54:49.760
one of the things that you'll find at a
company.

00:54:49.760 --> 00:54:52.178
Somebody does a great job and they say

00:54:52.178 --> 00:54:55.690
let's give them something for doing that
great job.

00:54:55.690 --> 00:55:00.362
You have this incredible experience
they'll say I can't

00:55:00.362 --> 00:55:03.900
I, I don't wanna make the others feel bad.

00:55:05.240 --> 00:55:08.692
Well if you can't identify what they did
and justify the

00:55:08.692 --> 00:55:12.519
great thing they did by rewarding them, he
shouldn't do it.

00:55:12.519 --> 00:55:17.580
But if you can do it, you should do it and
make it transparent as can be.

00:55:17.580 --> 00:55:21.890
It doesn't mean the others can't get
something someday for something.

00:55:21.890 --> 00:55:23.680
But this idea of leveling everything, it's
like the

00:55:23.680 --> 00:55:25.929
companies that give 100 or 500 stock
options to everybody.

00:55:25.929 --> 00:55:27.910
[INAUDIBLE] statement plan.

00:55:27.910 --> 00:55:31.450
It's like having a dental plan.

00:55:31.450 --> 00:55:34.620
I mean, what do you gain if everybody gets
it?

00:55:34.620 --> 00:55:36.290
There, there's no evaluation.

00:55:36.290 --> 00:55:38.560
There's no differentiation.

00:55:38.560 --> 00:55:42.630
People, people know who's, who's ca, ca,
carrying the freight.

00:55:42.630 --> 00:55:45.740
And they know who is not carrying the
freight.

00:55:45.740 --> 00:55:49.962
I, i, in our company, for example, despite
this system, after seven

00:55:49.962 --> 00:55:54.270
years, the top people thought we were
tough enough on weak performance.

00:55:54.270 --> 00:55:58.698
90 plus percent of the blind su, survey
